@startuml
title Smart Campus - Domain class diagram (revised)

class Student {
  - studentId : String
}

class Room {
  - roomId : String
  - blocked : boolean
  + isAvailable(start : DateTime, end : DateTime) : boolean
  + block() : void
  + unblock() : void
}

class Booking {
  - bookingId : String
  - start : DateTime
  - end : DateTime
  - status : BookingStatus
  + durationMinutes() : int
  + overlaps(other : Booking) : boolean
  + cancel() : void
}

enum BookingStatus {
  ACTIVE
  CANCELLED
}

Student "1" -- "0..*" Booking : makes >
Room "1" -- "0..*" Booking : is reserved by >

note right of Booking
  R1: start is in the future and 0 < duration <= 2 hours.
  R2: active bookings for the same room must not overlap.
  Back-to-back bookings (end = next start) are allowed (A1).
  R2 cannot be expressed by a multiplicity.
  cancel(): status becomes CANCELLED; only ACTIVE bookings count for R2.
  R4: a successfully created booking produces a confirmation (US-04).
end note

note right of Room
  R3: while blocked is true, the room accepts no new booking.
  Existing bookings stay active (assumption A2).
end note

@enduml